  "worked_solution": "This is a rational function, so it is continuous at all points in its domain. To find its domain, we start by factoring the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\frac{x+5}{{x}^{2}+2x-15} \\\\  & =\\frac{x+5}{{x}^{2}+5x-3x-15} \\\\  & =\\frac{x+5}{(x+5)(x-3)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{x-3},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere $x\\ne -5.$\n\nThis function is continuous everywhere except at the excluded points $x=-5$ and $x=3.$\n\nTherefore, the domain consists of the union of the intervals $(-\\infty ,-5),$ $(-5,3),$ and $(3,\\infty ),$ namely\n\n$$\n(-\\infty ,-5)\\cup (-5,3)\\cup (3,\\infty )\n$$\n\nand the function is also continuous on this union of intervals.",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
